  "name": "Measles (Rubeola) Antibody IgM",
  "code": "MEASLES IGM",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Measles Antibody Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>IgG Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgG antibodies indicates immunity to the measles virus. It suggests that the person has been previously infected with measles or has received the measles vaccine, and their immune system has developed antibodies to protect against future infections.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>IgM Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgM antibodies suggests a recent or acute measles infection. It indicates an ongoing or recent infection with the measles virus. However, false positive IgM results are possible, and confirmatory testing is necessary to confirm the diagnosis.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Both IgG and IgM Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>Simultaneous presence of both IgG and IgM antibodies may indicate a recent measles infection or a reactivation of a previous infection. Further evaluation is required to determine the specific stage and nature of the infection.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Both IgG and IgM Antibodies Negative</div></td><td><div>A negative result for both IgG and IgM antibodies indicates no current or previous exposure to the measles virus and no immunity. It means the person is susceptible to measles infection.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
